# Hermetic ETL sample (N-Triples) — entity IRIs use graph.onta.sh default base shape.
# Pin ONTA_IRI_BASE if classify_triple host-sensitive paths are under test; mapper
# uses package prefixes but attrs/onto detection is path-based for most cases.

<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Person> .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Alice" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Person/attrs/email> "a@example.com" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Person/attrs/city_town> "SF" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Guest/attrs/status> "vip" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Person/attrs/status> "active" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Organization/acme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://graph.onta.sh/types/Organization> .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Organization/acme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acme" .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/onto/works_at> <https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Organization/acme> .
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/onto/source> "csv" .
# Skipped companion-style multi-segment attrs tail
<https://graph.onta.sh/entities/Person/alice> <https://graph.onta.sh/attr_meta/Person/email/source_url> <https://example.com/src> .
